</aside>

# Straw polls # {#straw-polls}

## Proposed EWG polls ## {#proposed-polls}

These are proposed direction polls for P1219R3. They have not been taken.

1. We want named homogeneous function parameter packs for C++29: one trailing pack, ordinary parameter initialization, and an invented constant template parameter for its count, independently of unnamed-syntax reclamation.
2. We want to remove deprecated comma-less C varargs in C++29 and reclaim the spelling for unnamed homogeneous function parameter packs.

The first poll can proceed without the second. Approval of the second poll would make parameter names optional. If EWG requests separate scheduling, removal can move to a separate paper without changing the named feature.

