The Belfast poll failed. The public Kona record identifies objections to template-introducing syntax and to conflict with explicit-specialization syntax. It does not establish why the later Belfast poll failed. R3 renews the case with current-language comparisons, the invented count parameter, pack-indexing interactions, and a separate compatibility decision for unnamed packs. [[P1219-EWG-RECORD]]

# Implementation experience # {#implementation}

P1219R2 links to an experimental <a href="https://github.com/Bekenn/clang/tree/func-parm-packs">Clang branch</a>. [[P1219R2]] Its tests use an earlier <code>template &lt;&gt;</code> primary-template spelling. [[P1219-CLANG-TESTS]]

