# Wording # {#candidate-rules}

All modifications are relative to the C++26 working draft N5050. [[N5050]] Prose edits are marked inline. Added text is green, removed text is red, and unchanged text is unmarked. Only inline deletions are struck through. Whole additions and removals use + and - blocks. Code and grammar changes use a single block, with unchanged lines shown once.

The core wording describes the named homogeneous-pack feature. For that independently selectable feature, add to the homogeneous-pack declaration requirements below:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane">
<p class="diff-label">Addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>A homogeneous function parameter pack shall have a <span class=grammar>declarator-id</span>.</ins></p></div>
</div>
</div>

Retain the existing comma-less grammar, unnamed-ellipsis disambiguation, and deprecation text. If EWG also approves reclamation, omit that name requirement and apply [[#wording-reclamation]]. The remaining count, deduction, and identity rules are shared by both choices.

## Signatures ## {#wording-signatures}

No change is proposed to <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/defns.signature.spec">[defns.signature.spec]</a> or <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/defns.signature.member.spec">[defns.signature.member.spec]</a>. The invented count is a template argument and is already covered by their existing template-argument component. A separate pack-length component would duplicate it.

## Template-id identity ## {#wording-template-id-identity}

No additional count-identity condition is proposed for <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.type#1">[temp.type]/1</a>. Explicitly supplied and deduced values for the invented constant template parameter use ordinary template-argument equivalence. The same template and equivalent arguments identify the same specialization. An omitted count still has to be deduced before a specialization is identified. An empty explicit template-argument list does not imply a zero count.

## Lambdas ## {#wording-lambdas}

In <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/expr.prim.lambda.general#6">[expr.prim.lambda.general]/6</a>, insert after the first sentence:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane">
<p class="diff-label">Context and addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><p>A lambda is a generic lambda if the <span class=grammar>lambda-expression</span> has any generic parameter type placeholders (<a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/dcl.spec.auto">[dcl.spec.auto]</a>), or if the lambda has a <span class=grammar>template-parameter-list</span>.</p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>A <span class=grammar>lambda-expression</span> is also a generic lambda if its <span class=grammar>parameter-declaration-clause</span> declares a homogeneous function parameter pack (<a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.variadic">[temp.variadic]</a>).</ins></p></div>
</div>
</div>

In <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/expr.prim.lambda.general#6">[expr.prim.lambda.general]/6</a>, append to Example 4:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane diff-code">
<p class="diff-label">Addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><div><ins><code nohighlight>// OK: a generic lambda</code></ins></div></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><div><ins><code nohighlight>auto w = [](int... i) { return (0 + ... + i); };</code></ins></div></div>
</div>
</div>

In <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/expr.prim.lambda.closure#5">[expr.prim.lambda.closure]/5</a>, insert after the first sentence:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane">
<p class="diff-label">Context and addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><p>The closure type for a <span class=grammar>lambda-expression</span> has a public inline function call operator (for a non-generic lambda) or function call operator template (for a generic lambda) (<a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/over.call">[over.call]</a>) whose parameters and return type are those of the <span class=grammar>lambda-expression</span>'s <span class=grammar>parameter-declaration-clause</span> and <span class=grammar>trailing-return-type</span> respectively, and whose <span class=grammar>template-parameter-list</span> consists of the specified <span class=grammar>template-parameter-list</span>, if any.</p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>If the <span class=grammar>lambda-expression</span> declares a homogeneous function parameter pack, the function call operator template has the invented constant template parameter introduced by the abbreviated-function-template rules (<a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/dcl.fct">[dcl.fct]</a>). It follows any explicitly declared template parameters and invented type parameters. Its type and interpretation are specified in <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.variadic">[temp.variadic]</a>.</ins></p></div>
</div>
</div>

<aside class=issue>
