## Variadic templates ## {#wording-variadic}

In <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.variadic#2">[temp.variadic]/2</a>, insert after the first sentence:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane">
<p class="diff-label">Context and addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><p>A function parameter pack is a function parameter that accepts zero or more function arguments.</p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>For a <span class=grammar>parameter-declaration</span> that declares a function parameter pack, its <em>parameter pattern</em> is the <span class=grammar>parameter-declaration</span> with the ellipsis in its declarator or <span class=grammar>abstract-declarator</span> removed. The unexpanded packs in the parameter pattern are determined after introducing any template parameter corresponding to a placeholder type in the declaration.</ins></p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>If the parameter pattern contains no unexpanded packs, the declaration declares a <em>homogeneous function parameter pack</em>. Otherwise, it declares a function parameter pack that is a pack expansion whose pattern is the parameter pattern. This classification is determined before substituting template arguments from an enclosing templated entity and is not changed by that substitution.</ins></p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>A homogeneous function parameter pack shall declare parameters of the function declared by a function declaration or of a lambda's function call operator template.</ins></p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>A homogeneous function parameter pack has an associated invented constant template parameter, its <em>count parameter</em>. The type of the count parameter is the type of a <code>sizeof</code> expression (<a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/expr.sizeof">[expr.sizeof]</a>). The argument for the count parameter is the <em>pack count</em> and specifies the number of function parameters introduced by the pack. A homogeneous function parameter pack shall be the last parameter in its <span class=grammar>parameter-declaration-clause</span>. That clause shall not contain a C-varargs ellipsis or another function parameter pack.</ins></p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>The type of each parameter introduced by a homogeneous function parameter pack is obtained from its parameter pattern by substitution and the parameter type adjustments specified in <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/dcl.fct">[dcl.fct]</a>. Substitution into the element type is performed even when the pack count is zero. The parameters so introduced are function parameters for all other purposes. The value of a <code>sizeof...</code> expression naming this pack is the argument for its count parameter.</ins></p></div>
</div>
</div>

Replace <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.variadic#6.1">[temp.variadic]/6.1</a> with:

<blockquote class=wording-inline>
<p>In a function parameter pack <ins>that is a pack expansion </ins>(<a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/dcl.fct">[dcl.fct]</a>)<del>;</del><ins>,</ins> the pattern is <del>the <span class=grammar>parameter-declaration</span> without the ellipsis</del><ins>its parameter pattern</ins>.</p>
</blockquote>

Replace the first three sentences of <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.variadic#8">[temp.variadic]/8</a> with:

<blockquote class=wording-inline>
<p><del>A pack whose</del><ins>An occurrence of a</ins> name <del>appears</del><ins>denoting a pack is unexpanded in a construct unless it is</ins> within the pattern of a pack expansion <del>is expanded by that pack expansion</del><ins>contained in that construct</ins>.<ins> A pack is unexpanded in a construct if the construct contains at least one such occurrence. An occurrence that declares a pack is not considered when determining unexpanded packs.</ins></p>
<p><del>An appearance of the name of</del><ins>Each occurrence of a name denoting</ins> a pack is <del>only expanded</del><ins>expanded only</ins> by the innermost <del>enclosing </del>pack expansion<ins> whose pattern contains that occurrence</ins>. The pattern of a pack expansion shall <del>name</del><ins>contain</ins> one or more <del>packs that are not expanded by a nested pack expansion; such packs are called </del>unexpanded packs<del> in the pattern</del>.</p>
<p>All of the packs expanded by a pack expansion shall have the same number of arguments specified. An appearance of a name of a pack that is not expanded is ill-formed.</p>
</blockquote>

Retain the remaining requirements of paragraph 8, the other expansion patterns in paragraph 6, and the element interpretations in paragraph 9.

Replace the <code>all</code> example in <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.variadic">[temp.variadic]</a> with:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane diff-code">
<p class="diff-label">Context and changes</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-delete"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">-</span><div><del><code nohighlight>template&lt;typename ...Args&gt;</code></del></div></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-delete diff-mixed"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">-</span><div><code nohighlight>bool all(<del>Args </del>...args) {</code></div></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert diff-mixed"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><div><code nohighlight>bool all(<ins>bool</ins>...<ins> </ins>args) {</code></div></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><div><code nohighlight>    return (... &amp;&amp; args);</code></div></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><div><code nohighlight>}</code></div></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><div><code nohighlight>&#160;</code></div></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><div><code nohighlight>bool b = all(true, true, true, false);</code></div></div>
</div>
</div>

Within the instantiation of <code>all</code>, the returned expression expands to <code>((true &amp;&amp; true) &amp;&amp; true) &amp;&amp; false</code>, which evaluates to <code>false</code>.

## Dependency ## {#wording-dependency}

Under the proposal, a function type containing a homogeneous function parameter pack depends on the invented count parameter until its argument is determined, even when the element type is non-dependent. A <code>sizeof...</code> expression naming the pack is value-dependent while that argument is undetermined. Substitution of the count follows ordinary template substitution. Unrelated expressions do not become dependent merely because the function has a homogeneous pack.

<aside class=issue>
<p><strong>Ian: wording. Jan: review. Eczbek: implementation.</strong> Check dependency when the element type is fixed but the count is unknown. Test substitution failure in pack expressions, indexing, and count constraints, including an invalid indexed element type at count zero.</p>
</aside>

## Deduction ## {#wording-deduction}

In <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.deduct.general#1">[temp.deduct.general]/1</a>, insert before Example 1:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane">
<p class="diff-label">Context and addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><p>When a function template specialization is referenced, all of the template arguments shall have values. The values can be explicitly specified or, in some cases, be deduced from the use or obtained from default <span class=grammar>template-argument</span>s.</p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>For a function template that declares a homogeneous function parameter pack, the argument for its count parameter shall be determined. The argument can be explicitly specified or deduced as described in <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.deduct.call">[temp.deduct.call]</a> and <a href="https://timsong-cpp.github.io/cppwp/n5050/temp.deduct.type">[temp.deduct.type]</a>. After substitution, the pack introduces the number of function parameters specified by that argument, each formed from its parameter pattern. Explicit specification and deduction of equivalent count arguments identify the same specialization under the ordinary template-argument equivalence rules.</ins></p></div>
</div>
</div>

<aside class=issue>
<p><strong>Ian: wording. Jan: review. Eczbek: implementation.</strong> Check substitution order and failure handling. Apply an explicit count before matching parameters and deduce an omitted count before checking constraints that use it. Include preceding template parameter packs. We still need to complete these rules.</p>
</aside>

